      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da2e60e7_846cd64e",
        "filename": "common/usb_charger.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1478788
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-30T15:40:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds interesting but I\u0027m thinking that doing that may end up introducing some fuzzy behavior like \"bug X happens every num_port events\" rather than \"bug X only happens on port N\". Do you have a specific use case in mind?",
      "parentUuid": "76c1cae5_e5c163ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "a568c525efd82352504879d08ccffd152b0df6a3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5085eaf_13a93fc6",
        "filename": "common/usb_charger.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-31T16:23:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My thinking was to avoid starving the higher number ports.  Especially for Chromebooks with 3 or more type-C ports.\n\nI suppose we already have this issue now with the separate threads for each port - the lower port numbers are a higher priority.",
      "parentUuid": "da2e60e7_846cd64e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "a568c525efd82352504879d08ccffd152b0df6a3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
